    "findings": [
      "All eleven boards were directly read. 22r5 shows projected teal/orange depth bars on separate gray bases. The finite near=1 far=100 example d=100/99-100/(99z) gives z=1,2,10,100 and d=0,.505,.909,1; orange inverse-depth bars replace the teal bars in timed stages. Labels distinguish this numerical example from floating-point precision claims.",
      "22r6 shows a gray projected surface with a growing teal normal arrow and a separate violet RGB display surface. n=(0,0,1) maps to (.5,.5,1) via (n+1)/2 and is explicitly not surface albedo. Actual engine compression/channel layout remains separately qualified.",
      "22r7 separates projected surface position from light-space depth; a yellow arrow grows across them. lightMatrix*position and depth comparison are distinct, with bias/cascade/virtual-page selection qualified for the actual consuming pass.",
      "22r8 shows the screen-depth boundary on a gray projected plane, and orange/green fallback blocks outside it. Teal screen traversal and branching fallback arrows grow in stages; the caption does not claim every reflection uses one identical tracing path.",
      "Integer transitions are correct at 831/832, 1730/1731 and 2585/2586, with adjacent ±2 frames reviewed. The final frame 3489 is populated, text remains readable and top/front/side faces remain visible.",
      "Clean source samples contain no burned narration captions. Full moving review and final composition/caption/mixed-ASR approval remain pending."
